 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Ear and Ease, as if the couch were heaven,\nCall me of earth to welcome my spirit,\nAnd that I be mine; but never again\nThis first, this last solitude alone.\nBut when in hope I think on Heaven,\nWhen Heaven's calling hinders me away,\nI feel myself sickened with despair;\nBecause of Heaven's solitary way,\nEre some one has call'd me, I stand alone.\nNor can my soul such time absolve away;\nIt will not long suffice to wander\nWith all its light and bliss of delight,",
